### Sanity / pass-fail checks
1. **Warm-up absorbs compile:** instrument: time first step call separately vs steady-state steps; assert (steady-state per-step time) < (first-step time) by a large factor (e.g., ≥ 10×) or simply that SPS over the timed window is stable across trials within a seed (IQR small relative to median). Also detect absence of recompile warnings by scanning JAX log; set `JAX_DEBUG_NANS` no. Use `jax.jit` and confirm only one compilation via `jax.experimental`? Simpler: run warmup count high enough (200) and confirm per-trial SPS stable (trial-to-trial CV < some threshold, e.g. 5%).
