# Experiment Design (design-only \u2014 no runs, no claimed results)\n\nImplements the agreed fixed-requirement chain (setup_4, setup_5, setup_9): **MPE Simple Spread**, **random actions**, **steps-per-second** as the metric, with the locked decisions from the first pass. Everything below is a protocol, not an outcome.\n\n## 1. Protocol (step-by-step run procedure)\n\n### A. Session setup (once, logged)\n1. Record machine context: `lscpu` (CPU model, cores, threads, flags incl. AVX2/AVX512), kernel (`uname -a`), OS image/build, Python `3.14.4`, and `pip freeze` (exact jax / jaxlib / pettingzoo / gymnasium / numpy versions).\n2. Pin process: `os.sched_setaffinity(0, PHYSICAL_CPUS)` to a fixed physical core set (excluding logical siblings where possible); assert `os.sched_getaffinity() == pinned` (sanity check in \u00a73).\n3. Cap thread pools consistently for both impls: `OMP_NUM_THREADS`, `OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS`, `MKL_NUM_THREADS`, `NUMEXPR_NUM_THREADS` set to the pinned core count; disable NVIDIA/GPU (`CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=\"\"`), force `jax.config.update(\"jax_platform_name\",\"cpu\")`.\n4. Log the affinity set, env vars, and versions to the run log before any measurement.\n\n### B. Shared action tensor (identical actions for both impls)\n- One `numpy.random.RandomState(seed)` draws `actions_all = rng.choice(V, size=(warmup+T, n_agents, 5))` (one-hot in the env-native encoding \u2014 see note below), shape `(2200, 3, 5)` for the default `warmup=200, T=2000`. Rows `[0:warmup]` feed warm-up, rows `[warmup:warmup+T]` feed the timed loop. Identical rows are fed to both implementations (`jnp.asarray(row)` for JaxMARL, `{agent: row[i]}` for PettingZoo). Same `seed` is also passed to both env resets.\n- Encoding note (run-time verified, not assumed-in-canon): JaxMARL MPE discrete actions may expect one-hot `(3,5)` or integer indices depending on pinned version; generate `actions_all` in the installed env's native form and confirm equality of the exact values consumed by both (sanity check in \u00a73). Equality of *load* is the requirement; exact state trajectory need not match (agreed assumption).\n\n### C. Per-implementation timing helper (skeleton)\n\n```python\nimport time, jax, jax.numpy as jnp\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef measure_sps(env, warmup, T, actions_all, step_fn, reset_fn, agents=None):\n    \"\"\"env: ready-made impl-specific handle; returns (sps, elapsed, n_steps, log).\"\"\"\n    # agents passed only for PettingZoo (dict key order), None for JaxMARL\n    state, obs = reset_fn(seed=SEED)\n\n    # --- warm-up: no wall-clock recorded ---\n    idx = 0\n    for _ in range(warmup):                    # consumes rows [0:warmup]\n        a = actions_all[idx]\n        done = step_fn(state, a, idx)          # impl-specific adapter, see below\n        idx += 1\n\n    # --- timed loop: perf_counter only around step calls ---\n    start = time.perf_counter()\n    for _ in range(T):                         # consumes rows [warmup:warmup+T]\n        a = actions_all[idx]\n        done = step_fn(state, a, idx)\n        idx += 1\n    elapsed = time.perf_counter() - start\n\n    return T / elapsed, elapsed, T, state        # sps, seconds, steps, final state\n```\n\n**JaxMARL adapter** (functional API, shape-explicit):\n```python\nfrom jaxmarl.environments.mpe.simple_spread import SimpleSpread\nenv = SimpleSpread()\njstep = jax.jit(env.step) if not is_jitted(env.step) else env.step   # is_jitted via __wrapped__/pytree check; log which\ndef reset_fn(seed):\n    return env.reset(jax.random.PRNGKey(seed))   # returns (obs, state) in documented JaxMARL API; adapt to version's arity, log it\ndef step_fn(state, a, i):\n    global_state = state\n    obs, state, rew, dones, infos = jstep(state, jnp.asarray(a))   # a is (3,5); returns new (obs, state, ...)\n    return dones\n```\n- Fixed action shape `(3,5)` throughout \u2192 no mid-timing recompilation (locked decision b).\n- Compile soak: before the per-seed warm-up, one `jstep(state, sample)` call to force XLA compilation *outside* any timed region.\n\n**PettingZoo adapter** (parallel_env, shape-explicit):\n```python\nfrom pettingzoo.mpe.simple_spread_v3 import parallel_env\nenv = parallel_env(render_mode=None, max_cycles=warmup + T + 50)   # no truncation inside the window (see \u00a73 check)\ndef reset_fn(seed):\n    obs, infos = env.reset(seed=seed)\n    return (obs, infos), obs\ndef step_fn(state, a, i):\n    adict = {agt: a[j] for j, agt in enumerate(AGENTS)}   # AGENTS = list(env.agents), frozen after reset (n_agents=3)\n    obs, rew, term, trunc, infos = env.step(adict)\n    return any(term.values()) or any(trunc.values())\n```\n- `max_cycles` set so the episode cannot truncate during warm-up + timed window (Simple Spread has no natural terminator under random actions; this keeps the timed loop branch-free \u2014 no `reset` inside the timed region).\n- PettingZoo's per-step Python/dict overhead is part of the measured engine cost (agreed assumption 6).\n\n### D. Per-seed procedure (5 seeds)\nFor each seed: (1) draw `actions_all`; (2) create env; (3) compile soak (JaxMARL only); (4) 200-step warm-up (untimed); (5) run 5 timed trials of T=2000, each returning SPS; (6) keep env from overflowing (no early termination per above); (7) close/log. Trials within a seed reuse the same env state so warm state is representative; each trial is a fresh perf_counter window.\n\n## 2. Run matrix\n| Dim | Value | Justification |\n|---|---|---|\n| Impls | JaxMARL `simple_spread` vs PettingZoo `simple_spread_v3` (parallel) | the fixed comparison |\n| Seeds | 5 (`42,77,123,2048,9999`) | covers PRNG/init variation without cost overrun |\n| Trials/seed/impl | 5 | 25 measurements per impl; enough for stable median + bootstrap CI |\n| T (timed steps/trial) | 2000 | ~1\u20132 s/trial even for the slower impl; \u2265 per-trial resolution |\n| warmup | 200 (plus 1-call compile soak for JaxMARL) | \u226b per-step latency (~200\u2013500 \u00b5s PettingZoo); fully absorbs compile/JIT + torch/numpy thread warm-up |\n| Shared actions | one `(2200,3,5)` RandomState tensor per seed, identical rows to both | isolates engine speed from RNG cost |\n| n_agents, action space | 3, discrete 5 (native encoding) | fixed target |\n| Reported per cell | SPS, elapsed s, per-step \u00b5s, start/end obs-hash (advance proof), done-in-window flag | the per-cell record |\n\nTotal cells: 2 impls \u00d7 5 seeds \u00d7 5 trials = 50 SPS values plus metadata. Expected wall-clock: JaxMARL total run is dominated by the one-time compile per seed (seconds) and then fast step calls; PettingZoo at ~2k steps/trial \u2248 25 trials \u2248 tens of seconds; whole matrix minutes-level. Executable on CPU-only hardware (see \u00a74).\n\n## 3. Analysis plan\n**Pass/fail sanity checks (must pass before trusting numbers):**\n1. **Warm-up absorbed compile:** per-seed per-trial SPS is stable (intra-seed CV across the 5 trials < ~5%); also log first-step vs steady-state per-step time ratio (expect steady-state \u226a first-step) and scan the JAX log for recompile warnings (`jax` recompilation messages / \"XlaRuntimeError\") \u2014 any recompile mid-timed-window \u2192 mark seed invalid.\n2. **No recompile under fixed shapes:** shapes `(3,5)` constant; compile count = 1 per seed (verified via `jax` compilation counter if available, else absence of recompile warnings).\n3. **All agents step every call:** PettingZoo `len(env.agents)==3` and `adict` keys == `env.agents` every step; JaxMARL accepts `(3,5)` and state advances (obs-hash differs between consecutive steps).\n4. **Action-load equality:** `np.array_equal` of consumed vs provided `actions_all` rows sampled at \u22653 timesteps per seed/trial for both impls.\n5. **No termination mid-window:** no `done`/`trunc` True (PettingZoo) and no done flags (JaxMARL) during timed loop (guaranteed by `max_cycles` + non-terminating task; assert anyway).\n6. **Pinning active:** `os.sched_getaffinity() == pinned`; run log captured. **Repeat sanity:** re-run seed 42 once end-to-end; SPS within noise of the first run.\n\n**Aggregation & answer:**\n- Per impl: median, IQR (and MAD), mean\u00b1std of the 25 SPS values; convert to per-step \u00b5s.\n- Primary statistic: **median SPS ratio** `R = med(SPS_jaxmarl) / med(SPS_pettingzoo)`, with a **bootstrap 95% CI** on R (resample trials within seed, ~10,000 resamples) \u2014 CI excluding 1 supports \"beats\"; report both the ratio and the CI, never a scalar claim.\n- Because trials are seed-paired (shared actions/init), also report the paired per-seed mean-SPS differences with a paired bootstrap CI; SPS is non-Gaussian so prefer bootstrap/Wilcoxon over t-test. Report as machine-specific, not a general guarantee.\n- Outlier rule: any trial with elapsed flagged by `> 3\u00d7MAD` from the seed median due to scheduler preemption is reported + rerun, not silently dropped; raw and cleaned values both reported.\n\n**Reporting table columns:** `impl | seed | trial | T | warmup | elapsed_s | sps | per-step_us | start_obs_hash | end_obs_hash | done_in_window | checks(1\u20136)` then the aggregated rows (`impl | median | IQR | mean | std | CV | min | max | bootstrap_CI(ratio)`) and the final comparison row `R | 95% CI | verdict(CI excludes 1) | machine_ctx`.\n\n## 4. Controls & limitations\n**Controlled (by design):** identical shared action tensor + init seed (action-load equality); one-step definition (full parallel transition, all 3 agents); timing scope = `perf_counter` around the timed loop only (construction, reset, compile soak, 200-step warm-up excluded); JAX forced to CPU with fixed shapes (no mid-timing recompile); `max_cycles` set so PettingZoo cannot truncate mid-window; process affinity pinned + thread caps; single node; versions frozen via `pip freeze` in the log; CPU flags/`lscpu` captured.\n\n**Controlled but imperfect / unverifiable in design-only mode:**\n- CPU frequency scaling / turbo state and thermal state \u2014 cannot be forced; mitigated by affinity + repeats + outlier rerun, but SPS remains machine- and load-specific.\n- Scheduler preemption from other tenants on shared cores \u2014 mitigated by pinning, 5 trials, outlier rule; not eliminated.\n- Exact pinned-version internals: whether the installed JaxMARL `step` is pre-jitted, the true obs/action encoding, and the PettingZoo `max_cycles`/loop structure are verified **at run time** (checks in \u00a73), not assumed now \u2014 this sandbox has no source, no packages, and network disabled, so they are design-recalled only.\n- XLA instruction selection (AVX path), first-touch page effects, and per-step Python overhead in PettingZoo are measured as-is (part of fair engine cost).\n\n**Feasibility:** a real run needs `jax`, `jaxlib` (CPU wheel), `pettingzoo[mpe]` (pulls `gymnasium`), and `numpy` \u2014 suggested pins to freeze at run time (recalled, not verified locally): `jax>=0.4.x`+matching CPU `jaxlib`, `pettingzoo>=1.23`, `gymnasium>=0.28`, `numpy>=1.24`. All are pure-CPU x86-64 compatible; the whole matrix is CPU-only, so `gpu_enabled=false` in this environment is consistent, but dependencies are **not preinstalled and network is off here**, so execution would happen in an instrumented, package-installed environment \u2014 which this design-only task does not claim (track.md: \"repositories and compute are not required\").\n\n**Fixed requirements (non-negotiable):** Simple Spread target, random actions, SPS metric, one-step = full parallel transition, shared-action protocol, pinned context, and no executed/claimed results. **Assumptions (agreed, from first pass):** semantic equivalence of the two envs' spaces; exact API/version behavior per installed JaxMARL/PettingZoo (run-time-verified, not source-verified here); availability of a compatible CPU environment to execute; comparable-not-identical state trajectories under identical action load.", "assumptions": ["Semantic equivalence of JaxMARL simple_spread vs PettingZoo simple_spread_v3 spaces (3 agents, discrete 5-action, comparable obs) per public docs \u2014 not source-verified in this empty workspace.", "Exact installed-version API arity/encoding (JaxMARL reset/step return shapes, one-hot vs integer actions, whether step is pre-jitted) is recalled from public knowledge and pinned/verified at run time, not assumed in canon.", "A compatible CPU-only environment with jax/jaxlib/pettingzoo/gymnasium/numpy installed exists to execute the design; this sandbox has none (no source, no packages, no network).", "Identical shared action tensor guarantees equal action load but not identical state trajectories across impls.", "One step = one full parallel env transition (all 3 agents act once); PettingZoo per-step Python/dict overhead is part of the fair engine cost being measured.", "Simple Spread does not naturally terminate under random actions; PettingZoo max_cycles is set to avoid truncation inside the timed window, keeping the timed loop branch-free.", "No experiment is executed and no results are claimed: the deliverable is a protocol and analysis plan only."], "evidence": "Workspace inspection (this pass): /workspace contains only task.json; no JaxMARL/PettingZoo/MPE source, no requirements/pins; find across the filesystem for jaxmarl/pettingzoo/mpe returned only unrelated system binaries. Environment verified: bubblewrap, network disabled, Python 3.14.4, no relevant packages in `pip list`, 224 cpu_affinity_count, gpu_enabled=false, deps not preinstalled; task.json confirms track.md = 'Design-only task; repositories and compute are not required'. These constrain the design to recall JaxMARL functional API (init(rng)/step(state,actions), jit on step, batched (3,5) actions, reset/step arities) and PettingZoo parallel_env (reset(seed=...), step(dict), max_cycles) as run-time-verified assumptions rather than local facts. Approvals from the first pass: one step = one full parallel transition; SPS = perf_counter over timed loop only with compile soak + 200-step warm-up excluded, JAX forced CPU, fixed shapes; single RandomState (2200,3,5) action tensor shared identically; 5 seeds \u00d7 5 trials per impl; affinity/thread-cap/version context pinned. Skeleton and checks derive from these locked decisions.", "summary": "Deliver full design-only experiment: protocol, matrix, analysis, controls", "stage": "result", "uncertainties": ["Exact JaxMARL SimpleSpread reset/step return arity and discrete-action encoding depend on the pinned installed version and can only be confirmed at run time (sanity checks in the design); not verifiable here.", "XLA CPU recompilation cannot be fully pre-verified; mitigated by fixed shapes, a compile soak, and a recompile-warning scan, but only the real run settles it.", "Wall-clock SPS is machine- and load-specific; even with affinity pinning, frequency scaling, thermal state, and tenant contention are not fully controllable.", "PettingZoo parallel_env internal iteration order of agents across reset must be stable for shared-action alignment; the design freezes agent order after reset and asserts key equality.", "Recommended package pins are recalled from public releases, not verified against this environment."]}", "origin": "completion"}, "llm_response_id": "chatcmpl-d1382cc0605846b7b40b948c96143ed2", "security_risk": "UNKNOWN", "critic_result": null, "summary": "Deliver full design-only experiment: protocol, matrix, analysis, controls", "kind": "ActionEvent"}
